{
  "slug": "pith",
  "name": "Pith",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Automatic token optimization for Claude Code. Compresses tool output 40–60%, shows a live token meter in the statusline, auto-compacts at 70% context, builds a self-updating project wiki, and supports structured output modes (LEAN/ULTRA/PRECISE) to extend session length 3×.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills**, **4 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `pith` (Adaptive output compression), `pith-arch` (One-shot architecture decision format), `pith-commit` (One-shot commit message generator), `pith-debug` (One-shot structured debug format), `pith-graph` (Run the Pith wiki graph generator for the current project), `pith-install` (Install Pith into Claude Code), `pith-plan` (One-shot planning format), `pith-review` (One-shot structured code review), and 4 more\n- **Commands** (4): `budget` (Set a hard token ceiling per response (e.g), `focus` (Load only the sections of a file relevant to the current question, reducing context noise), `pith-graph` (Run the Pith wiki graph generator for the current project), `pith` (Control Pith token compression modes and access structured output formats, wiki, and status)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install pith@claude-community` from `abhisekjha/pith`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 12,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 4
  },
